# BUG: when a list future has no consistent timeline, the "show why" guesses crash:
# z3.z3types.Z3Exception: Z3 expression expected, because paradox.py substitutes a whole
# list of future variables into z3.substitute. The one case that matters - a list paradox -
# is the one that cannot be explained.
bits 8
d = future(d, 2)
d[0] = d[0] + 1
